    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d7">

                <pb facs="pm_d7-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d7-1"/>

                <head>PM–7. Letter from the Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for International
                    Security Affairs (Irwin) to the Assistant Secretary of State for Inter-American
                    Affairs (Rubottom)<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d7-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-09-22">September 22,
                        1958</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Mr. Rubottom:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Our letter of 27 November 1956<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d7-f2"/> requested that
                    negotiations be resumed with the Republic of Panama for the acquisition of two
                    radar sites to be used for anti-aircraft purposes. It has now been determined
                    that for the present no action should be taken to modernize the anti-aircraft
                    defenses of the Panama Canal. It is requested therefore, that no further effort
                    be made at this time to secure the sites in question.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="pm_d7-f3"/></p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Deputy Assistant
                    Secretary</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d7-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d7-f1-content">
